<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Full Expert Evaluation Tiered Rubric</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below in <a href="#A3.T4" title="In Appendix C Full Expert Evaluation Tiered Rubric ‣ QEDBench: Quantifying the Alignment Gap in Automated Evaluation of University-Level Mathematical Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is the verbatim text of the tiered rubric provided to our expert evaluators (PhD students and holders) as the
template for the problem-specific expert rubrics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Detailed Tiered Rubric for Human Expert Evaluation.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Score</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="A3.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T4.5.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.5.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Detailed Description</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">1.0</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.5.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T4.5.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.5.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Fully Complete.</span><span id="A3.T4.5.2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> A fully complete and correct proof is presented. There are no errors at any point in calculations, computations, or proofs of sub-claims/lemmas. The proof can be followed easily. All statements that are not common knowledge are rigorously proved.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">0.9</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.5.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T4.5.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.5.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Correct with Oversight.</span><span id="A3.T4.5.3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> The proof is nearly accurate except for one small flaw/oversight (e.g., omission of a small edge case). The model may fail to completely justify finer points (hand-waving). Crucially, compared to the 0.75 case, the flaw must be an </span><span id="A3.T4.5.3.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">oversight</span><span id="A3.T4.5.3.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> (failed to explain a fact) as opposed to a logical </span><span id="A3.T4.5.3.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">error</span><span id="A3.T4.5.3.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">0.75</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T4.5.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.5.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Correct with Minor Error.</span><span id="A3.T4.5.4.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> The proof is nearly accurate. There might be a small mistake in a claim or calculation, but it is effectively isolated and does not snowball throughout the entire proof. Includes proofs with small incorrect assumptions or inconsistencies, provided there is only one such issue.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">0.5</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T4.5.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.5.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Significant Flaws.</span><span id="A3.T4.5.5.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> The proof is lacking in more than one of the areas listed above. If a model makes multiple small mistakes, or a single medium-sized mistake which has an effect that carries on to other parts of the proof, this score is granted.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">0.25</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.5.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T4.5.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.5.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Severe Failure.</span><span id="A3.T4.5.6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> The proof is severely lacking in multiple areas. Either multiple small mistakes are littered throughout, or there is a large mistake at the beginning that snowballs and invalidates the rest of the proof. The output showcases little understanding of the problem mechanics.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T4.5.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">0.0</span></th>
<td id="A3.T4.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A3.T4.5.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.5.7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Non-existent/Hallucinated.</span><span id="A3.T4.5.7.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> The proof is completely wrong or non-existent. It may prove a different statement entirely or showcase no understanding of the context. Relies on made-up facts or fallacies to build a false proof.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Example Full Rubrics</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we provide the full text of examples of both the <span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expert Correctness</span> and
<span id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Course-Specific</span> rubrics. More rubrics can be found in our public GitHub repository <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">QEDBench, 2026</a>)</cite>
The rubrics illustrate how the evaluations differ between evaluating for course-specific items versus correctness based on expert domain knowledge.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Graph Expansion Path Existence (Algorithms Problem 10)</h3>

<section id="A4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.1.1 </span>Problem Statement</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a graph <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> consisting of <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> vertices. Assume there exists a constant <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for every subset <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> with cardinality <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|=n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|=n/2</annotation></semantics></math>, the set of neighbors satisfies <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(S)|\geq n/2+\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(S)|\geq n/2+\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> be a positive integer, and consider subsets <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1},\dots,W_{k}\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1},\dots,W_{k}\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|W_{i}|\geq(1-\alpha)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|W_{i}|\geq(1-\alpha)n</annotation></semantics></math>. Prove that it is possible to construct a path <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}\in W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}\in W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.1.2 </span>Expert Correctness Rubric</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A4.I1" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.0 (Fully Complete)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The solution constructs a valid inductive reachability argument and explicitly or implicitly establishes the backtracking step to produce the path.</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1.ix1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expansion Consequence:</span> Correctly notes or uses the consequence that <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math> (derived from <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(S)|\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(S)|\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>) and implies <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\alpha)n\geq n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\alpha)n\geq n/2</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring each <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough to contain an <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math>-subset.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Set Definitions:</span> Defines reachable sets/layers <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (or equivalent structures):</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}=W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}=W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i+1}=N(U_{i})\cap W_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i+1}=N(U_{i})\cap W_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inductive Proof:</span> Proves by induction that <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U_{i}|\geq n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U_{i}|\geq n/2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> (ensuring non-emptiness).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U_{i}|\geq n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U_{i}|\geq n/2</annotation></semantics></math>, explicitly restricts attention to a subset <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|=n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|=n/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Uses monotonicity (<math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(S)\subseteq N(U_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(S)\subseteq N(U_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>) to infer <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(U_{i})|\geq|N(S)|\geq n/2+\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(U_{i})|\geq|N(S)|\geq n/2+\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applies inclusion–exclusion with <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|W_{i+1}|\geq(1-\alpha)n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|W_{i+1}|\geq(1-\alpha)n</annotation></semantics></math> to conclude:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U_{i+1}|=|N(U_{i})\cap W_{i+1}|\geq(n/2+\alpha n)+(1-\alpha)n-n=n/2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U_{i+1}|=|N(U_{i})\cap W_{i+1}|\geq(n/2+\alpha n)+(1-\alpha)n-n=n/2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Path Reconstruction:</span> Constructs the actual path from the non-empty set <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> via backtracking (e.g., pick <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}\in U_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}\in U_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then pick neighbor <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k-1}\in U_{k-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k-1}\in U_{k-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, etc.) or by defining the sets <math id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as ”endpoints of valid paths.”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix1.I1.i10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Consistency:</span> All inequalities, set containments, and cardinality bounds are mathematically consistent.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9 (Minor Oversight)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The essential argument is correct and rigorously structured, but contains a minor technical oversight or handwave that does not undermine the core logical validity.</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1.ix2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Correctly uses <math id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i+1}=N(U_{i})\cap W_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i+1}=N(U_{i})\cap W_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and the inclusion–exclusion bound, but omits a small technical justification, such as:</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Does not explicitly mention <math id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math> (but calculation holds).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Ignores floor/ceiling issues for <math id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is odd.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Omits the explicit description of the backtracking step, though the existence of predecessors is an immediate consequence of the set definitions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Slight imprecision regarding whether <math id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(S)</annotation></semantics></math> includes <math id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, provided the size calculations remain valid under the student’s definition.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Constraint:</span> The submission must still present a logically valid chain implying <math id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i+1}\neq\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i+1}\neq\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.I1.ix2.I2.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.75 (Small Mistake)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The plan is mostly correct but contains one localized error (computational or logical) that requires repair but does not derail the method.</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1.ix3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Calculation Error:</span> Computes the lower bound for <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(U_{i})\cap W_{i+1}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(U_{i})\cap W_{i+1}|</annotation></semantics></math> incorrectly (e.g., forgets inclusion–exclusion and claims it is simply <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math>), yet argues for non-emptiness in a way that remains logically coherent with minor corrections.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Monotonicity Gap:</span> Forgets to pass to an <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math>-subset <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and incorrectly applies the expansion hypothesis directly to a set <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;n/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note:</span> If the student explicitly states <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(S)\subseteq N(U_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(S)\subseteq N(U_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> elsewhere or clearly intends this step despite the omission, score as <span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9</span>. If the logic implies they believe the hypothesis applies directly to sets larger than <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math> without justification, score here.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reconstruction Flaw:</span> Muddles the final path selection (e.g., chooses <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}\in U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}\in U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> independently rather than ensuring adjacency), but the definitions of <math id="A4.I1.ix3.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> allow for a correct backtracking repair.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.5 (Multiple Mistakes / Conceptual Gap)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multiple issues or a significant conceptual gap affects the core proof, though relevant ideas (induction, expansion) are present.</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1.ix4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Failed Invariant:</span> Attempts induction but fails to justify <math id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|U_{i}|\geq n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|U_{i}|\geq n/2</annotation></semantics></math> (or non-emptiness) due to:</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applying expansion to sets of wrong sizes without reduction.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fatal errors in inclusion–exclusion resulting in negative or meaningless bounds.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unjustified assumptions that ”large sets have large neighborhoods” beyond the specific <math id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math> guarantee.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Greedy Failure:</span> Proposes a greedy construction (pick <math id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, etc.) without proving that a valid neighbor exists at each step (fails to connect expansion to the specific choice).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix4.I4.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Misapplied Theorems:</span> Invokes Hall’s Theorem or Menger’s Theorem but models the graph incorrectly (e.g., fails to define the layered structure or verify the specific conditions required by the expansion property).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.25 (Severely Lacking)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Major early misunderstanding or gap makes the argument largely unusable.</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1.ix5.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ignored Expansion:</span> Does not use the <math id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(S)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(S)|</annotation></semantics></math> expansion property in any substantive way (e.g., treats it merely as a minimum degree condition).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Size Fallacy:</span> Claims the path exists solely because <math id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|W_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|W_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math> are large, ignoring edge existence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unproven Advanced Results:</span> Relies entirely on an unproven or misquoted advanced result (e.g., Expander Mixing Lemma) without verifying hypotheses.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix5.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vague Handwaving:</span> States ”by expansion there is a path” without inductive set construction or verifiable counting.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0 (Completely Wrong)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No meaningful attempt or the argument is unrelated to the problem.</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I1.ix6.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hallucinated theorems (e.g., ”Any expansion implies Hamiltonicity”).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Constructs objects that do not satisfy <math id="A4.I1.ix6.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}\in W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}\in W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or do not form a path.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I1.ix7" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">General Notes &amp; Checkpoints</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I1.ix7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A4.I1.ix7.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Graph Type:</span> Accept either undirected or directed graphs if the student consistently uses the appropriate out-neighborhood definition.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rounding:</span> If <math id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is odd, fully rigorous solutions should clarify <math id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor n/2\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor n/2\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lceil n/2\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lceil n/2\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>. Minor rounding imprecision is a <span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9</span> issue unless it breaks the inequalities.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Arithmetic Check:</span> The key quantitative checkpoint is the arithmetic:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n/2+\alpha n)+(1-\alpha)n-n=n/2" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n/2+\alpha n)+(1-\alpha)n-n=n/2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Grader must explicitly verify the student achieves this cancellation to prove the intersection is size <math id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backtracking:</span> The backtracking/predecessor step is technically required to turn non-empty sets into an explicit sequence. However, if the definition of <math id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., reachable vertices) encodes the existence of a predecessor, explicit listing of the backward selection is a minor detail (score <span id="A4.I1.ix7.I7.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9</span> if missing).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_leader"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.1.3 </span>Course-Specific Rubric</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A4.I2" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A4.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.0 (Fully Complete)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Uses only course-appropriate graph/induction arguments to prove the existence of a constrained walk across <math id="A4.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> layers. The proof must contain the following structural elements:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2.ix1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Feasibility/Rounding:</span> Clarifies <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> must be even or handles rounding (<math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor n/2\rfloor,\lceil n/2\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor n/2\rfloor,\lceil n/2\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>). Implicitly or explicitly notes <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math> is required for the problem constraints to make sense.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reachable Sets Definition:</span> Defines a sequence of reachable sets (e.g., <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{1}:=W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{1}:=W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i+1}:=W_{i+1}\cap N(R_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i+1}:=W_{i+1}\cap N(R_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inductive Invariant:</span> Proves <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R_{i}|\geq n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R_{i}|\geq n/2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> by induction:</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Base Case:</span> <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R_{1}|=|W_{1}|\geq(1-\alpha)n\geq n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R_{1}|=|W_{1}|\geq(1-\alpha)n\geq n/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inductive Step:</span> Uses the hypothesis on a subset <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math> to show <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(R_{i})|\geq n/2+\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(R_{i})|\geq n/2+\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math> via monotonicity (<math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(R_{i})\supseteq N(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(R_{i})\supseteq N(S)</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Intersection:</span> Uses <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap B|\geq|A|+|B|-n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap B|\geq|A|+|B|-n</annotation></semantics></math> to show <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|W_{i+1}\cap N(R_{i})|\geq(1-\alpha)n+(n/2+\alpha n)-n=n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|W_{i+1}\cap N(R_{i})|\geq(1-\alpha)n+(n/2+\alpha n)-n=n/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Walk Construction:</span> Explicitly constructs the walk <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{1},\dots,v_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> by backtracking from <math id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}\in R_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}\in R_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> or maintaining parent pointers.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix1.I1.i8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Justification:</span> All set inequalities and theorem applications are explicitly justified.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9 (Minor Oversight)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is essentially correct and demonstrates full understanding, but contains a minor oversight that does not undermine the logic:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2.ix2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rounding:</span> Does not explicitly address <math id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> being odd, but the logic clearly adapts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backtracking:</span> Omits the explicit backtracking step but clearly establishes that <math id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i+1}\subseteq N(R_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i+1}\subseteq N(R_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> implies the existence of valid predecessors.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expansion Logic (Minor):</span> Applies the expansion hypothesis directly to <math id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R_{i}|\geq n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R_{i}|\geq n/2</annotation></semantics></math>) without explicitly stating ”take a subset <math id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math>,” <span id="A4.I2.ix2.I2.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">provided</span> the student demonstrates awareness of this monotonicity logic elsewhere in the proof.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I2.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.75 (Small Mistake)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I2.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The approach is correct (layered reachable sets + induction), but contains a specific error that requires a local fix:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2.ix3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Calculation Error:</span> Miscomputes the intersection lower bound (e.g., constant factor error) but the conclusion of non-emptiness remains valid if corrected.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expansion Logic (Gaps):</span> Applies the expansion hypothesis directly to <math id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> without subset justification and <span id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">without</span> indicating awareness that the hypothesis is restricted to sets of size exactly <math id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Constraint Derivation:</span> Assumes <math id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math> without noting it follows from the hypothesis (since <math id="A4.I2.ix3.I3.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2+\alpha n\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2+\alpha n\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I2.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.5 (Multiple Mistakes / Partial Progress)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I2.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Partially correct but misses key justifications or contains medium-sized logical errors:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2.ix4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Connectivity vs Walk:</span> Proves existence of edges between <math id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> pairwise but fails to ensure they can be connected into a single continuous walk (fails to maintain a reachable set invariant).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Greedy Approach:</span> Attempts to pick <math id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> step-by-step greedily without a lookahead or set-maintenance mechanism, often leading to unjustified claims that the walk won’t get stuck.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Incorrect Expansion:</span> Assumes expansion holds for <span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">all</span> sets (not just size <math id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n/2</annotation></semantics></math>) or fails to show <math id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(R_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(R_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough to intersect <math id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Single Vertex Induction:</span> Tries to define <math id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> based on the neighborhood of a single vertex <math id="A4.I2.ix4.I4.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> rather than a set, breaking the size invariant.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I2.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.25 (Severely Lacking)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I2.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Major conceptual mismatch or fundamental errors:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2.ix5.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simple Path Confusion:</span> Argues for a simple path (distinct vertices) using diameter/counting arguments, ignoring that <math id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrary and repetitions may be needed.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Neighborhood Misinterpretation:</span> Misinterprets the condition (e.g., counts edges instead of neighbors, assumes regularity/completeness).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vague Intuition:</span> Claims ”expansion implies connectivity” without any set-based proof or demonstration of non-empty intersections.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix5.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Black Box:</span> Uses non-course machinery (e.g., probability/spectral arguments) without justification or correctness.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I2.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0 (Completely Wrong)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I2.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No meaningful progress or reliance on forbidden tools:</p>
<ul id="A4.I2.ix6.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Invokes PCP theorem, advanced circuit complexity, or Hall’s/Menger’s theorems in irrelevant ways.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Claims result is obvious or derived from contradictory assumptions (e.g., <math id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix6.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No valid invariant or construction method proposed.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I2.ix7" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">General Notes &amp; Checkpoints</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I2.ix7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A4.I2.ix7.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Walk vs. Path:</span> Since <math id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrary, the solution must construct a <span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">walk</span> (vertices may repeat). Insisting on a simple path is a conceptual error unless <math id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leq n</annotation></semantics></math> is explicitly assumed and distinctness is proved.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Key Lemma:</span> If <math id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R|\geq n/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R|\geq n/2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|N(R)|\geq n/2+\alpha n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|N(R)|\geq n/2+\alpha n</annotation></semantics></math>. This must be justified by monotonicity (<math id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subseteq R\implies N(S)\subseteq N(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subseteq R\implies N(S)\subseteq N(R)</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Key Counting:</span> The intersection bound <math id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A\cap B|\geq|A|+|B|-n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A\cap B|\geq|A|+|B|-n</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard course-appropriate method to show the sets intersect.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Allowed Tools:</span> Induction, BFS/Layered graph reachability, set algebra.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I2.ix7.I7.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forbidden Tools:</span> Advanced spectral graph theory, PCP theorem, or complexity theory constraints not covered in the course.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Alternating Permutations &amp; Eulerian Numbers (Combinatorics Problem 6)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we provide the full text of both the <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expert Correctness</span> and <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Course-Specific</span> rubrics for the Combinatorics problem described in the benchmark.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.1 </span>Problem Statement</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of permutations of numbers from <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> with exactly <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> descents. Prove that <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the alternating sum of numbers <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of alternating permutations of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.2 </span>Expert Correctness Rubric</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A4.I3" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A4.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.0 (Fully Complete &amp; Rigorous)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The solution provides a mathematically sound, complete, and rigorous proof establishing the identity. The argument must be self-contained, clearly defined, and handle all necessary cases (including parity).</p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Required Elements (One of the following primary routes):</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Route A: Sign-Reversing Involution (Preferred Combinatorial Proof)</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setup:</span> Correctly defines descent (<math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="des(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">des(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>) and interprets the sum <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math> as a signed sum over the symmetric group <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\pi\in S_{n}}(-1)^{des(\pi)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\pi\in S_{n}}(-1)^{des(\pi)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Involution Definition:</span> Defines an explicit map <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi:S_{n}\to S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi:S_{n}\to S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Well-Definedness:</span> Demonstrates that <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is an involution (<math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{2}=id" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{2}=id</annotation></semantics></math>) and is well-defined for all <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sign-Reversing Property:</span> Proves rigorously that if <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\pi)\neq\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\pi)\neq\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="des(\phi(\pi))=des(\pi)\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">des(\phi(\pi))=des(\pi)\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures the cancellation of non-fixed points.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fixed Points:</span> Correctly characterizes the fixed points of <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">·</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Shows fixed points correspond exactly to alternating permutations (e.g., no double ascents or descents).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation:</span> Calculates the sum over fixed points.</p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">·</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Identifies that for even <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, fixed points cancel or do not exist (sum is 0), OR correctly relates them to the problem statement if a specific convention allows otherwise.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">·</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Identifies that for odd <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, the sum is non-zero and equals <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i6.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm(\text{Number of Alternating Permutations})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Number of Alternating Permutations</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm(\text{Number of Alternating Permutations})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion:</span> Explicitly states the final identity with correct sign factors (e.g., <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{(n-1)/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{(n-1)/2}</annotation></semantics></math>) and parity distinctions.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Route B: Generating Functions (Analytic Proof)</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definitions:</span> Introduces the Eulerian polynomial <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}(t)=\sum E(n,k)t^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}(t)=\sum E(n,k)t^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EGF Usage:</span> Uses the standard Exponential Generating Function (EGF) for Eulerian polynomials (e.g., related to <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-t}{e^{x(t-1)}-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-t}{e^{x(t-1)}-t}</annotation></semantics></math>). Citation of this standard form is acceptable if accurate.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Substitution:</span> rigorously performs the substitution <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simplification:</span> Simplifies the resulting expression correctly (typically involving hyperbolic functions or <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tan(x)+\sec(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tan(x)+\sec(x)</annotation></semantics></math> analogues).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coefficient Extraction:</span> Relates the coefficients of the simplified series back to the definition of alternating permutations (<math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion:</span> Explicitly derives the relationship, noting that the sum vanishes for even <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and matches the alternating permutation count (with sign adjustment) for odd <math id="A4.I3.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9 (Minor Oversight)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The solution is fundamentally correct and mathematically convincing, but contains a negligible imperfection.</p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Examples of acceptable oversights:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The involution is correct, but the handling of a boundary case (e.g., index <math id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=n</annotation></semantics></math> in a “first double ascent” definition) is slightly imprecise, though the intended fix is obvious.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Uses a standard EGF formula without derivation or specific citation, provided the application is algebraically flawless.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Omits an explicit statement about the global sign factor <math id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{(n-1)/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{(n-1)/2}</annotation></semantics></math> in the final line, though the work preceding it implies the correct sign.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix2.I2.i1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Minor notational ambiguity regarding “alternating” (up-down vs. down-up) that does not affect the validity of the core logic.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I3.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.75 (Small Mathematical Mistake)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I3.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The approach is correct, but the execution contains a specific mathematical error that affects the details (sign, count, or parity) without invalidating the entire method.</p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Typical issues:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Involution Error:</span> The map <math id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is conceptually sound, but the proof that <math id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="des" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">des</annotation></semantics></math> changes by exactly <math id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math> fails for a specific local configuration (e.g., miscounting descents during a swap).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fixed Point Misidentification:</span> Correctly identifies that fixed points are alternating but fails to distinguish between up-down and down-up types, leading to a factor-of-2 error.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parity Error:</span> Claims a non-zero value for even <math id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> without justification, or misses the cancellation for even <math id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> entirely.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algebraic Error:</span> In the GF route, makes a sign error during the <math id="A4.I3.ix3.I3.i1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=-1</annotation></semantics></math> substitution or simplification, leading to an incorrect constant factor.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I3.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.5 (Substantial Gaps or Multiple Errors)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I3.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The solution demonstrates partial understanding and attempts a valid method, but fails to provide a complete proof due to significant logical gaps or multiple errors.</p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Typical issues:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Flawed Involution:</span> The proposed map is not proven to be an involution, is not well-defined, or does not reliably flip the parity of the descent number.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assertion vs. Proof:</span> Asserts that the fixed points are alternating permutations without any argument linking the involution’s condition (e.g., “no double ascents”) to the definition of alternating permutations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">conceptual Confusion:</span> Confuses Eulerian numbers with other statistics (e.g., inversions) or uses an incorrect identity as a starting point.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Unjustified Leaps:</span> Uses specialized theorems (e.g., “sec + tan counts alternating perms”) <span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span> EGF formulas without justification, making the logic difficult to verify.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conditional Correctness:</span> The result is only correct for odd <math id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, with no mention or incorrect handling of even <math id="A4.I3.ix4.I4.i1.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I3.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.25 (Severely Lacking)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I3.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The solution provides minimal relevant content, relying on assertions or fundamentally incorrect definitions.</p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix5.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Typical issues:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">States the identity as a fact without derivation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proposed involution is clearly not invertible or does not reverse signs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Misdefines fundamental concepts (descents, alternating permutations) in a way that makes the proof meaningless.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Provides only empirical checks (e.g., “works for <math id="A4.I3.ix5.I5.i1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math>”) with no general argument.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I3.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0 (Completely Wrong)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I3.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No mathematical progress.</p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix6.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Examples:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Irrelevant combinatorics or unrelated formulas.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">“Hallucinated” theorems.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix6.I6.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Blank or non-mathematical text.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I3.ix7" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Key Checks for Graders</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I3.ix7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A4.I3.ix7.I7" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parity:</span> Does the student acknowledge that for <span id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">even</span> <math id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, the alternating sum <math id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math> typically vanishes? If they claim it equals <math id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (alternating perms) for even <math id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, is there a non-standard definition of <math id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> or a sign error?</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sign Factor:</span> For <span id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">odd</span> <math id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, the sum usually equals <math id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{(n-1)/2}E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{(n-1)/2}E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Check for the presence of this sign factor or a justification for its absence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fixed Points:</span> If using an involution, the fixed points must be “permutations with no double ascents/descents.” This is the definition of alternating permutations. A proof that merely asserts this link without showing equivalence (e.g., <math id="A4.I3.ix7.I7.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i}&lt;\pi_{i+1}&gt;\pi_{i+2}\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}&lt;\pi_{i+1}&gt;\pi_{i+2}\dots</annotation></semantics></math>) is a 0.5-level response.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_leader"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.3 </span>Course-Specific Rubric</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="A4.I4" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="A4.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.0 (FULLY COMPLETE)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A rigorous, course-appropriate proof that explicitly handles the parity of <math id="A4.I4.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and connects the alternating sum to alternating permutations.</p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Required Observable Elements:</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correct Setup:</span> Identifies the target sum as <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}(-1)=\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}(-1)=\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parity/Sign Handling:</span> Explicitly states and proves that:</p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">even</span> <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}(-1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}(-1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">odd</span> <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{n}(-1)|=E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{n}(-1)|=E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> (the count of alternating permutations).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(Note: Allow for variations in sign conventions/indexing, provided they are consistent).</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rigorous Proof (One of the following methods):</span></p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A) Sign-Reversing Involution:</span> Defines a map on permutations that changes the descent number by <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math> (flipping the sign of the weight). Proves the map is a valid involution. Identifies fixed points correctly (none for even <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>; alternating permutations for odd <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(B) Generating Functions:</span> Uses the correct EGF for Eulerian polynomials. Evaluates at <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Shows this matches the EGF for alternating permutations (specifically the tangent numbers for odd <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> for even <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>). Justifies analytic steps at the formal power series level.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">*</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(C) Recurrence Relations:</span> Derives a recurrence for the sum <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}=\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}=\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math> from the standard Eulerian recurrence. Shows <math id="A4.I4.ix1.I1.i1.I1.i3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> matches the recurrence for alternating permutations (up to sign/parity) and verifies base cases.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I4.ix2" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.9 (MINOR OVERSIGHT)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I4.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Essentially correct and conceptually sound, but contains a minor lapse in rigor or notation.</p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sloppy Constants:</span> The connection to alternating permutations is correct, but the specific sign factor (e.g., <math id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{(n-1)/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{(n-1)/2}</annotation></semantics></math>) is missing or incorrect.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Brief Even Case:</span> Correctly identifies that the even <math id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> case sums to 0, but provides a weak justification (e.g., “by symmetry” without showing the symmetry <math id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}(t)=t^{n-1}A_{n}(1/t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}(t)=t^{n-1}A_{n}(1/t)</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Minor Involution Gap:</span> The involution strategy is correct, but the proof that descents change by exactly <math id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math> is glossed over.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Base Cases:</span> Minor omission of base case verification (e.g., checks <math id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math> but not <math id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.I4.ix2.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I4.ix3" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.75 (SMALL MISTAKE)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I4.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The strategy is appropriate and course-specific tools are used, but a genuine mathematical error is present.</p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Flawed Involution:</span> The proposed map is not strictly sign-reversing as stated (e.g., undefined for certain permutations or fails to be an involution), though the intent is clear and fixable.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recurrence Error:</span> Derives the recurrence for the alternating sum but makes an algebraic/indexing error (e.g., mishandling boundary terms <math id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=n-1</annotation></semantics></math>), leading to a faulty intermediate expression.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generating Function Error:</span> Quotes an incorrect formula for the Eulerian EGF but proceeds to evaluate at <math id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=-1</annotation></semantics></math> correctly based on that incorrect formula.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parity Confusion:</span> Proves the result for odd <math id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> correctly but incorrectly claims the same non-zero formula applies to even <math id="A4.I4.ix3.I3.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, ignoring the cancellation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I4.ix4" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.5 (MULTIPLE MISTAKES)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I4.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Partial progress with relevant ideas, but significant gaps in logic or definitions prevent a complete proof.</p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix4.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">No Connection:</span> Calculates <math id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{n}(-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{n}(-1)</annotation></semantics></math> or sets up the sum but fails to prove it counts alternating permutations (asserts the result without proof).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Failed Involution:</span> Attempts an involution but fails to define the map, prove it is an involution, or identify the fixed points.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conceptual Error:</span> Confuses “number of descents” with the specific “descent set,” arguing that knowing <math id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> determines if a permutation is alternating (it does not).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recurrence Failure:</span> Starts with the Eulerian recurrence but fails to manipulate the alternating sum into a solvable form.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parity Ignored:</span> Completely fails to distinguish between even and odd <math id="A4.I4.ix4.I4.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in a globally incorrect claim.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I4.ix5" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.25 (SEVERELY LACKING)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I4.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Major misunderstanding of the problem or reliance on inappropriate tools.</p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix5.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition Errors:</span> Misdefines Eulerian numbers or alternating permutations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contradiction:</span> Claims <math id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)=E_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum(-1)^{k}E(n,k)=E_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> without addressing the obvious contradiction for small even <math id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> (where the sum is 0).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Black Box:</span> Uses advanced algebraic machinery (Descent Algebras, Representation Theory) without derivation or explanation, bypassing the required combinatorial coursework.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Empirical Only:</span> Provides only a table of values checking the identity for small <math id="A4.I4.ix5.I5.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> with no general proof structure.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
<dt id="A4.I4.ix6" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.0 (COMPLETELY WRONG)</span></span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="A4.I4.ix6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No relevant work or completely incoherent.</p>
<ul id="A4.I4.ix6.I6" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">No attempt to relate Eulerian numbers to alternating permutations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proof consists of unrelated or false statements (e.g., treating <math id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math> as binomial coefficients).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">•</span></span> 
<div id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I4.ix6.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Empty submission.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Full Automated Evaluator Prompts</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure reproducibility, we provide the exact prompt templates used in our <span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Evaluator-Solver Matrix</span>. The prompt construction logic injects specific constraints based on whether the evaluator is grading against the <span id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Course-Specific Rubric</span> or the <span id="A5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Expert Rubric</span>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>System Prompts</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The system prompt enforces the persona and the output format.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST4" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="LST4.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">System Prompt Logic for Evaluators</p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="LST4.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_figure_panel ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx55" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx55.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Base</span><span id="lstnumberx55.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx55.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Instruction</span><span id="lstnumberx55.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">:</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx56" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx56.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx56.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">You</span><span id="lstnumberx56.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">are</span><span id="lstnumberx56.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx56.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">strict</span><span id="lstnumberx56.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">academic</span><span id="lstnumberx56.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">evaluator</span><span id="lstnumberx56.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">for</span><span id="lstnumberx56.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">graduate</span><span id="lstnumberx56.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">-</span><span id="lstnumberx56.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">level</span><span id="lstnumberx56.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">mathematics</span><span id="lstnumberx56.21" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">.</span><span id="lstnumberx56.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">Grade</span><span id="lstnumberx56.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">based</span><span id="lstnumberx56.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">EXCLUSIVELY</span><span id="lstnumberx56.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">on</span><span id="lstnumberx56.30" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.31" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">the</span><span id="lstnumberx56.32" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx56.33" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">rubric</span><span id="lstnumberx56.34" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">."</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx57" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
