rmal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\log 2}^{\infty}u^{-p}\,du</annotation></semantics></math>, but then notes (without resolving) that this converges only for <math id="A15.I6.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, so the proposed <math id="A15.I6.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> fails for general <math id="A15.I6.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. The student then attempts to “correct the construction” by redefining <math id="A15.I6.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A15.I6.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, but the solution is cut off before any integrability/non-integrability checks are completed. In particular, there is no finished proof that <math id="A15.I6.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in L^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A15.I6.i3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\notin L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\notin L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A15.I6.i3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq p</annotation></semantics></math>. Partial credit is warranted only for identifying the key integral test/substitution and noticing the convergence issue with the initial attempt.”</p>
</div></li>
