mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\log 2}^{\infty}u^{-p}\,du</annotation></semantics></math>, which diverges when <math id="A15.I6.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;p\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;p\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, so it fails to handle arbitrary <math id="A15.I6.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The student recognizes this problem (“we actually need <math id="A15.I6.i4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>”) but then abandons the argument and replaces <math id="A15.I6.i4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> with a different definition without carrying out the necessary integrability/non- integrability checks. No proof is given that the final (partially stated) function lies in <math id="A15.I6.i4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> while failing to lie in <math id="A15.I6.i4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A15.I6.i4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq p</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus there is some relevant setup and correct identification of the key integral test idea, but the solution is incomplete and not correct as written, justifying partial credit.”</p>
