oding="application/x-tex">g\in L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> or that <math id="A15.I6.i7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\notin L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\notin L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A15.I6.i7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq p</annotation></semantics></math>. The mathematical framework is partially correct, but no complete, verified construction is provided. The score of 0.25 reflects partial understanding of the approach but failure to deliver a complete rigorous proof.”</p>
