="application/x-tex">x\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> does not correctly yield a function in exactly <math id="A15.I6.i8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, as the student partially recognizes. The corrected construction involving <math id="A15.I6.i8.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x^{-1/p}(-\log x)^{-1/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{-1/p}(-\log x)^{-1/p}</annotation></semantics></math> near zero is also incomplete and lacks verification that it belongs to <math id="A15.I6.i8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> while excluding all other <math id="A15.I6.i8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> spaces. A correct solution would require a more sophisticated construction, typically combining behavior at both zero and infinity to exclude both <math id="A15.I6.i8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A15.I6.i8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="applic