or complete the verification that <math id="A15.I6.i20.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in L^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> but <math id="A15.I6.i20.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\notin L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\notin L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A15.I6.i20.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq p</annotation></semantics></math>. This omission renders the proof incomplete and mathematically insufficient, as the core construction and convergence arguments are absent. Overall, the partial setup warrants 0.25/1.0 for initial correctness, but the lack of a full, rigorous demonstration limits the score.”</p>
