<li id="A15.I6.i22" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A15.I6.i22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A15.I6.i22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A15.I6.i22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Judge: grok-4-0709 (course-specific-rubric.txt)</span> <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A15.I6.i22.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Author: deepseek-v2-prover</span> (Score 0.5): “The student’s initial construction of <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)</annotation></semantics></math> fails for <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, as the integral <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\log 2}^{\infty}u^{-p}\,du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\log 2}^{\infty}u^{-p}\,du</annotation></semantics></math> diverges when <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, incorrectly assuming convergence for all <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The attempted correction shifts to an interval near 0 with <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g(x)=x^{-1/p}(-\log x)^{-1/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=x^{-1/p}(-\log x)^{-1/p}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a step toward addressing integrability at the origin, but the solution abruptly ends without computing the <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math>-norm or verifying exclusion from other <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> spaces. This leaves the proof incomplete, as the student does not demonstrate that <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g\|_{p}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g\|_{p}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g\|_{q}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g\|_{q}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A15.I6.i22.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq p</annotation></semantics></math>. Partial credit is warranted for recognizing the need for logarithmic adjustments to control integrability, but the lack of rigorous verification and completion undermines the solution’s correctness.”</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A15.I6.i23" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
