<p id="A15.I6.i25.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A15.I6.i25.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Judge: qwen/qwen-max (rubric.txt)</span> <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A15.I6.i25.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Author: Claude Sonnet 4.5</span> (Score 0.5): “The student’s solution is on the right track by attempting to construct a function that is in <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> but not in <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq p</annotation></semantics></math>. However, the solution is incomplete as it does not fully define the function <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and lacks the calculation or argument to show that <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in L^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in L^{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\notin L^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\notin L^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\neq p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\neq p</annotation></semantics></math>. The student has set up the problem and chosen an appropriate <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, but the actual definition of <math id="A15.I6.i25.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and the necessary integrability conditions are not provided. Therefore, the solution is only partially correct, justifying a score of 0.5.”</p>
