<p id="A16.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A16.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Judge: gpt-5.2-pro (rubric.txt)</span> <math id="A16.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A16.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Author: o3-deep-research</span> (Score 0.5): “The solution correctly states the goal <math id="A16.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}(-1)^{k}E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}(-1)^{k}E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math> and begins a plausible approach by encoding alternation as local “correct inequality” conditions <math id="A16.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and invoking inclusion–exclusion. However, the argument is incomplete: it stops before carrying out inclusion–exclusion, identifying the sizes of the intersections <math id="A16.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcap_{i\in S}C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⋂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcap_{i\in S}C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, or connecting those counts to the Eulerian numbers <math id="A16.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E(n,k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E(n,k)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, there is no demonstrated bijection or counting step showing that the inclusion–exclusion terms correspond to permutations with a specified number of descents, so the key identity is not proved. Thus the submission shows some correct setup but does not reach a mathematically complete proof, warranting partial credit (0.5/1.0).”</p>
